    "text": "Hunting Blind, 2023\n Plastic, PVC, wood, zinc.",
    "alignment": "center"
  },
  {
    "_type": "archiveText",
    "_key": "txt48",
    "text": "CMFMFB and Hunting Blind are reproductions of structures found at a Carnegie Mellon University construction site and a recreational hunting ground, respectively, within a 10 mile radius of the Interburden exhibition space. Together in conversation, these two forms blur the discontinuity of Pittsburgh\u2019s working-class identity and its contemporary, tertiary economy. Throughout this work, repurposed vernacular photography from the 1970s-1990s serves as documentation of Pittsburgh's economic transition.",
    "alignment": "justify"
  },
